From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 07:05:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] census: QEMU's own small loads and stores of guest RAM
 reach the census

address_space_ld*/st* (ldl_phys, stl_le_phys and the like, and their
_cached_slow forms) read and write RAM through qemu_map_ram_ptr directly,
past flatview_{read,write}_continue_step where census_ram_access is: such an
access of a Coherent surface's armed page read the older bytes, and a write to
a held or armed page never reached the library. Each now calls
census_ram_access first, one relaxed load while nothing is tracked.

Left alone: address_space_{read,write}_cached's inline memcpy, whose only
user here is virtio's vring caches, which lie in the guest kernel's memory,
never in an IOSurface's pages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 system/memory_ldst.c.inc | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/system/memory_ldst.c.inc b/system/memory_ldst.c.inc
index a728b7737c..3239d04ca7 100644
--- a/system/memory_ldst.c.inc
+++ b/system/memory_ldst.c.inc
@@ -43,8 +43,12 @@ uint64_t glue(address_space_ldm_internal, SUFFIX)(ARG1_DECL, MemOp mop,
         r = memory_region_dispatch_read(mr, addr1, &val, mop, attrs);
     } else {
         /* RAM case */
+        void *ptr = qemu_map_ram_ptr(mr->ram_block, addr1);
+
         fuzz_dma_read_cb(addr, size, mr);
-        val = ldm_p(qemu_map_ram_ptr(mr->ram_block, addr1), mop);
+        /* LOCAL (Atlas): a Coherent surface's armed page is brought up to date first. */
+        census_ram_access(ptr, size, false);
+        val = ldm_p(ptr, mop);
         r = MEMTX_OK;
     }
     if (result) {
@@ -85,7 +89,11 @@ void glue(address_space_stm_internal, SUFFIX)(ARG1_DECL, MemOp mop,
         r = memory_region_dispatch_write(mr, addr1, val, mop, attrs);
     } else {
         /* RAM case */
-        stm_p(qemu_map_ram_ptr(mr->ram_block, addr1), mop, val);
+        void *ptr = qemu_map_ram_ptr(mr->ram_block, addr1);
+
+        /* LOCAL (Atlas): a Coherent surface's held or armed page hears of the write first. */
+        census_ram_access(ptr, size, true);
+        stm_p(ptr, mop, val);
         invalidate_and_set_dirty(mr, addr1, size);
         r = MEMTX_OK;
     }
